# Dataset: Loan Approval

**File:** `loan_approved.csv`
**Rows:** 614 loan applications
**Columns:** 13

## Source
Provided as part of my Data Analytics training at Naresh IT, Hyderabad. Used here for learning and portfolio purposes.

## Columns

| Column | Description |
|---|---|
| Loan_ID | Unique ID of the loan application |
| Gender | Male or Female |
| Married | Yes or No |
| Dependents | Number of dependents (0, 1, 2, 3+) |
| Education | Graduate or Not Graduate |
| Self_Employed | Yes or No |
| ApplicantIncome | Applicant's income |
| CoapplicantIncome | Co-applicant's income (0 if none) |
| LoanAmount | Loan amount requested |
| Loan_Amount_Term | Loan term in months |
| Credit_History | 1 = good credit history, 0 = poor credit history |
| Property_Area | Urban, Semiurban or Rural |
| Loan_Status (Approved) | Y = approved, N = not approved |

## Missing values in the original file
Gender 13, Married 3, Dependents 15, Self_Employed 32, LoanAmount 22, Loan_Amount_Term 14, Credit_History 50. These were handled in the notebook (see the main README for how).

## Note
This is the original, uncleaned file. The cleaned version is created by running the notebook.
